<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" modified="2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z" agent="claude" version="24.0.0" type="device"><diagram name="0. Concepts (read first)" id="page0"><mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1654" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="c2" value="Page 0 — The five ideas you need to read the other pages" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="20" width="900" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c3" value="Each box is one concept. Read left to right, top to bottom. Every later page assumes these." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="55" width="1100" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c4" value="&lt;b&gt;Pixel frame&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A normal video frame: an image of shape [3, H, W] (RGB colour channels, height, width). At 480×832 that is 3×480×832 ≈ 1.2 M numbers per frame. Too big to run a generative model on directly at 16+ FPS." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="100" width="340" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c5" value="&lt;b&gt;Latent&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A compressed version of the frame(s) that the model actually works on. Wan 2.1 and TAEHV compress 8× in width/height and 4× in time, keeping 16 channels. So 4 pixel frames at 480×832 become ONE latent of shape [16, 60, 104] ≈ 100 k numbers. ~50× smaller. Think of it as a thumbnail with 16 &#x27;colours&#x27; that carry structure instead of RGB." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="100" width="340" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c6" value="&lt;b&gt;VAE (encoder / decoder)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Variational Auto-Encoder: two small networks. Encoder: pixels → latent. Decoder: latent → pixels. &#x27;Tiny&#x27; VAEs like TAEHV trade quality for speed (decoder = 9.84 M params vs hundreds of millions for the full Wan VAE). This project is about the DECODER only: it sits at the END of the pipeline, and every frame the user sees goes through it." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="740" y="100" width="340" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c7" value="&lt;b&gt;Diffusion / denoising step&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The generative model (a &#x27;DiT&#x27;, diffusion transformer, 30 blocks for Wan 1.3B) does not draw an image in one shot. It starts from a noisy latent and predicts a cleaner one, repeatedly. Here the timestep schedule is 700 → 500 → 0 (config), i.e. --step 2 means two model passes per chunk. Video-to-video: the input video is encoded, noise is ADDED to a chosen level, then denoised while following the text prompt." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="310" width="340" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c8" value="&lt;b&gt;Causal / streaming + KV cache&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#x27;Causal&#x27; = a frame may only look at PAST frames, never future ones, so the system can emit output as input arrives (live webcam use). The DiT remembers the past through a KV cache (attention keys/values kept for the last few latents, num_kv_cache=6). TAEHV&#x27;s decoder remembers the past through &#x27;MemBlocks&#x27; (each layer keeps its previous-timestep output). Both mean: the work for one chunk depends on state left behind by the previous chunk." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="310" width="340" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c9" value="&lt;b&gt;Rank / pipeline parallelism&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With torchrun, each GPU runs one copy of the script called a &#x27;rank&#x27; (rank 0, rank 1, …). StreamDiffusionV2 splits the 30 DiT blocks across ranks like an assembly line: rank 0 does blocks [0, b0), the last rank does blocks [b_k, 30) and also decodes. Throughput = 1 / (slowest station). If the last station is slow because of decode, adding GPUs does not help. That is the core suspicion of this project." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="740" y="310" width="340" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c10" value="&lt;b&gt;Chunk&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The unit of work flowing through the pipeline: 4 pixel frames = 1 latent timestep (num_frame_per_block=1). So the decoder is called with T=1 latent at a time, and must produce 4 pixel frames from it." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="520" width="340" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c11" value="&lt;b&gt;Kernel launch / launch-bound&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every GPU operation (a conv, a cat, a cast) is a &#x27;kernel&#x27; the CPU must launch. Launching costs ~5–20 µs regardless of size. A tiny decoder on a tiny input runs hundreds of tiny kernels, and the GPU spends most of its time waiting for the CPU to issue the next one. That is &#x27;launch-bound&#x27;: the fix is fewer/larger kernels (batching, CUDA graphs, torch.compile), not a faster GPU." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="380" y="520" width="340" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram name="1. StreamDiffusion v1 (reference)" id="page1"><mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1654" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="c2" value="Page 1 — StreamDiffusion v1 (SD 1.5) per-frame loop: reference only, shows WHERE the VAE sits on the critical path" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="20" width="900" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c3" value="Input frame
(webcam / video)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="110" width="150" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c4" value="Preprocess
resize, normalize" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="210" y="110" width="150" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c5" value="Similarity filter
skip frame if ≈ previous" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="400" y="110" width="150" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c6" value="VAE encode
pixels → 4-ch 2D latent
[4, 64, 64]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="110" width="150" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c7" value="SDEdit noise
add noise to chosen level" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="780" y="110" width="150" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c8" value="Stream Batch
stack several frames at
different denoise levels" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="270" width="150" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c9" value="U-Net
one call per loop" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="210" y="270" width="150" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c10" value="Split batch
take the fully-denoised one" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="400" y="270" width="150" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c11" value="VAE decode
latent → pixels" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="270" width="150" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c12" value="Output frame" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="780" y="270" width="150" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="e13" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c3" target="c4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e14" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c4" target="c5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e15" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c5" target="c6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e16" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c6" target="c7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e17" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c7" target="c8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e18" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c8" target="c9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e19" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c9" target="c10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e20" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c10" target="c11"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e21" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c11" target="c12"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c22" value="&lt;b&gt;Why this page exists.&lt;/b&gt; v1 and V2 have the same shape: encode → denoise → decode, with the decoder as the last thing before the user sees a frame. v1 uses Stable Diffusion 1.5 latents: 4 channels, one image at a time (2D). TAEHV/Wan latents are 16 channels and cover 4 frames at once (3D, &#x27;video latents&#x27;). They are not interchangeable, so &lt;b&gt;no code in v1 is touched&lt;/b&gt; (/home/joshua/StreamDiffusion.git is a bare mirror). Everything in this plan happens in V2 (pages 2–4)." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="420" width="950" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram name="2. V2 multi-GPU pipeline" id="page2"><mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1654" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="c2" value="Page 2 — StreamDiffusionV2 rank-pipelined inference (streamv2v/inference_pipe.py). Stage 12 (red) is the decode under study." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="15" width="1300" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c3" value="One chunk = 4 pixel frames → 1 latent [1, 1, 16, 60, 104] at 480×832. --step 2 ⇒ each chunk makes 2 trips around the ring (denoise 700 → 500 → 0) before it is decoded. With 2 GPUs there are no middle ranks (dashed lane is empty)." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="45" width="1300" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c4" value="Rank 0  (GPU 0)  —  run_rank_0_loop" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=26;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;collapsible=0;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="95" width="1300" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c5" value="Middle ranks  (GPU 1 … N-2, optional)  —  run_middle_rank_loop" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=26;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;collapsible=0;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#333333;dashed=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="285" width="1300" height="120" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c6" value="Final rank  (GPU N-1)  —  run_final_rank_loop" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=26;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;collapsible=0;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="425" width="1300" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c7" value="1. Load 4-frame chunk
(load_mp4_as_tensor / webcam)
[1, 4, 3, 480, 832]" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="c4"><mxGeometry x="20" y="45" width="170" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c8" value="2. Wan VAE stream_encode
pixels → latent
[1, 1, 16, 60, 104]
(rank 0 only, timed as t_vae)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="c4"><mxGeometry x="220" y="45" width="190" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c9" value="3. Noise blend
mix latent with noise at
timestep 700 (noise_scale)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="c4"><mxGeometry x="440" y="45" width="170" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c10" value="4. DiT blocks [0, b0)
block_mode=&#x27;input&#x27;
KV cache for last 6 latents
(timed as t_dit)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="c4"><mxGeometry x="640" y="45" width="200" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c11" value="5. Async send →
send_latent_data_async
on com_stream" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="c4"><mxGeometry x="870" y="45" width="170" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="e12" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="c4" source="c7" target="c8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e13" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="c4" source="c8" target="c9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e14" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="c4" source="c9" target="c10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e15" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="c4" source="c10" target="c11"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c16" value="6. Receive ←
(wait on com_stream)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="c5"><mxGeometry x="220" y="40" width="170" height="65" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c17" value="7. DiT blocks [b_i, b_i+1)
(timed as t_dit)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="c5"><mxGeometry x="440" y="40" width="200" height="65" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c18" value="8. Async send →" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="c5"><mxGeometry x="870" y="40" width="170" height="65" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="e19" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="c5" source="c16" target="c17"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e20" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="c5" source="c17" target="c18"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c21" value="9. Receive ←
receive_latent_data_async
then wait_stream(com_stream)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="c6"><mxGeometry x="20" y="40" width="170" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c22" value="10. DiT blocks [b_k, 30)
block_mode=&#x27;output&#x27;
→ x0 prediction
(timed as t_dit)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;" vertex="1" parent="c6"><mxGeometry x="220" y="40" width="200" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c23" value="11. Send x0 back to rank 0
(ring: next denoising step
or next chunk&#x27;s context)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="c6"><mxGeometry x="450" y="40" width="190" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c26" value="results[i]
→ mp4 / browser" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="c6"><mxGeometry x="1140" y="40" width="140" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c27" value="12. DECODE  (SYNCHRONOUS)
vae.stream_decode_to_pixel(x0[[-1]])
Wan VAE today; TAEHV in Step 2
1 latent → 4 pixel frames" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="c6"><mxGeometry x="670" y="40" width="220" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c28" value="13. Host copy
(video*0.5+0.5).clamp → permute
→ .cpu().float().numpy()
= forced GPU↔CPU sync" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="c6"><mxGeometry x="920" y="40" width="200" height="80" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="e29" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="c6" source="c21" target="c22"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e30" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="c6" source="c22" target="c23"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e31" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="c6" source="c23" target="c27"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e32" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="c6" source="c27" target="c28"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e33" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="c6" source="c28" target="c26"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c34" value="Only fires when the chunk is fully denoised (processed ≥ num_steps·world_size − 1). Runs on the compute stream AFTER DiT and BEFORE the next receive: no overlap with anything." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;fontSize=9;fontColor=#b85450;" vertex="1" parent="c6"><mxGeometry x="670" y="125" width="450" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="e35" value="latents + x0 + step idx" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c11" target="c16"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="975" y="275"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e36" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c18" target="c21"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="975" y="415"/><mxPoint x="125" y="415"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e37" value="2-GPU case: rank 0 → final rank directly" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;dashed=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c11" target="c21"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1310" y="280"/><mxPoint x="1310" y="415"/><mxPoint x="125" y="415"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e38" value="ring send-back: denoised x0 becomes
input for the next denoising step" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;strokeColor=#9673a6;strokeWidth=2;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c23" target="c10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="565" y="640"/><mxPoint x="25" y="640"/><mxPoint x="25" y="75"/><mxPoint x="760" y="75"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c39" value="&lt;b&gt;Block scheduler (--schedule_block, _handle_block_scheduling)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fires ONCE after schedule_step iterations. Each rank all_gathers two numbers: t_dit (its DiT time) and t_total. compute_balanced_split moves DiT block boundaries so t_total is equal across ranks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;What t_total actually contains (verified in code):&lt;/b&gt; rank 0 = t_dit + encode t_vae; middle = t_dit; final = t_dit + decode t_vae (incl. host copy). All three are the &lt;i&gt;minimum&lt;/i&gt; observed value, not the mean." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="660" width="620" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="e40" value="rebalances b_k" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;dashed=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.3;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c39" target="c22"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="720" y="700"/><mxPoint x="720" y="645"/><mxPoint x="340" y="645"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c41" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 2 attaches here (stage 12)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Add TAEHVDecoderWrapper with the same stream_decode_to_pixel() contract; select with --vae {wan, taehv, taehv_parallel}. Encoder (stage 2) stays Wan." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="660" y="660" width="320" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c42" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 3 attaches here (stages 9–13)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;CUDA-event timers around receive-wait / DiT / decode / host copy on the final rank; dump per-iteration JSON per rank; compute pipeline period = max stage time." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1000" y="660" width="320" height="130" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c43" value="&lt;b&gt;Step 4 fixes to validate&lt;/b&gt;  H1 (primary) → make decode a real pipeline stage: side CUDA stream overlapping the next receive, or a dedicated decode rank; pinned non-blocking host copy instead of .cpu().numpy().   H2 → mean-based, periodic rebalance in the scheduler.   Only if Step 1&#x27;s tripwire fires → CUDA-graph / batch latents." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="660" y="805" width="660" height="95" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram name="3. TAEHV decoder &amp; hypotheses" id="page3"><mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1654" pageHeight="1169" math="0" shadow="0"><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="c2" value="Page 3 — TAEHV decoder (/home/joshua/taehv/taehv.py, arch taew2_1), the three meanings of &#x27;parallel&#x27;, and hypotheses H1–H3. Step 1&#x27;s sanity check runs here, standalone." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="15" width="1300" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c3" value="Decoder architecture (nn.Sequential, ~40 layers)" style="swimlane;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;startSize=26;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;collapsible=0;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="60" width="300" height="640" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c4" value="Input latent  N,T,16,60,104
(pre-normalized, no mean/std)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontColor=#333333;" vertex="1" parent="c3"><mxGeometry x="20" y="40" width="260" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c5" value="Clamp (tanh-ish squash)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="c3"><mxGeometry x="20" y="95" width="260" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c6" value="conv 16 → n_f0, ReLU" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" vertex="1" parent="c3"><mxGeometry x="20" y="135" width="260" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c7" value="Stage 1: MemBlock ×3
(recurrent — reads previous timestep)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;" vertex="1" parent="c3"><mxGeometry x="20" y="180" width="260" height="45" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c8" value="Upsample 2×
